<!-- OUTPUT TABLE -->
<TABLE border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>
	<TR>
		<TD align=center><FONT face=verdana size=1 color=#ff4500><B>To Join Clan Stormbringer</B></FONT></TD>
	</TR>

		<TR>
			<TD align=center><FONT face=verdana size=1 color=#ff4500>Last Altered - 5/2/2001 4:50:44 PM</FONT></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b>How to Join</b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'>The following describes the requirements and processes for becoming a member of the Clan Stormbringer. The intent of these requirements is to insure that the player is a proper fit for the guild, that the player is capable of fulfilling their responsibilities to guild and that the mission and organization of the guild serves the players interest.
Requirements

<ul>
<li>Recommended to have at least 1 character at level 45 or higher</li>
<li>Required be sponsored by a current member, in good standing, of the guild.</li>
 
<li>Required to read, understand and accept the guild mission statements and adopt the guild's core values.</li>

<li>Required to read, understand and accept the guild expectations of participation</li>

<li>Required to provide player information including a valid email address.</li>

<li>Required to be able to raise 2 resist up to 80/80 at a given time. The first resist is always Magic Resist. </li>

<li>Required have Howling Stones and Sebilis keys. </li>

<li>Required have Great Divide Tooth and Cobalt Scars Tooth</li></ul>
<p>The level requirement is a recommendation and not a hard requirement. Players below level 45 may be accepted into the guild by agreement of the council. Most of the events conducted by the Clan Stormbringer will designed for the participation of players at level 50 or above. And players under level 45 may find themselves not receiving the full benefits of membership.</p>

<p>The player's sponsor must be a member in good standing of the guild. This means that the sponsor is an active member of the guild who has completed their probationary period. A players' sponsor is their mentor during the player's probationary period. If the sponsor is not an active member of the guild, it is unlikely they can fulfill their responsibility to the player during this time.</p>


</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b></b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>The guild's mission statement and core beliefs must set the player's expectations of participation in the guild. The core beliefs form the basis of the guideline of conduct. </p>
<p>The same is true of the expectation of participation. Mutual support and cooperative effort are the foundation of the guild's mission. Loyalty and commitment are core values. A player's adoption of the guild's mission and acceptance of its core values will be reflected in their participation in guild activities.</p>
<p>The guild must be able to communicate with its members. A valid email account is necessary to promote that communication and promote the participation in guild events.</p>





</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b></b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>Through experience, the members of the guild's council have discovered that the ability of a player to raise their resists contributes significantly to success in the game. This requirement measures a player's ability to come prepared to participate in a guild event.</p>
<p>This is also true for the requirements for keys to Howling Stones, Sebilis, Great Divide and Cobalt Scars. A player does not need to have all these keys in their possession at the time they make their application. However, it is expected that they will have these keys by the end of their probationary period (30 days) with the guild.
Applying For Membership</p>
<p>A player who wishes to apply for membership into the Clan Stormbringer must complete and submit the membership form on the guild's web site. The player is required to provide their character name, Class, Level, E-Mail address and the player name of the sponsoring member. If the player does not have a sponsoring member, they may request the Guild Chancellor to assist in identifying a sponsor for the applicant.</p>



</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b></b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>The Chancellor of the guild will attempt to contact new applicants within 7 days of the submission for membership and make arrangements for an initial interview. In this interview the Chancellor will verify that the player has read the Charter of the guild, understands and accepts the Mission, Core Values, Expectations of Participation and the Guidelines of Conduct.</p>

</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b></b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>If the applicant has a sponsor, the Chancellor may choose to admit the applicant as a probationary member after the initial interview. An applicant will not be admitted without a sponsoring member. New applicants will maintain a probationary status for 30 days. At the end of the probationary period, the member must meet all requirements for membership of the guild. The council will then vote on the final acceptance of the player into the guild. </p>
</TD>
		</TR>
		
	
</TABLE><!-- END OUTPUT TABLE -->
		
